---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Shot from "../../components/Shot.astro";
import CtaBand from "../../components/CtaBand.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Culia Autos Case Study"
  description="How Forthmark Systems built the Culia Autos vehicle discovery website and admin system: inventory, saved cars, comparison, paid consultation booking, and client handover."
  image="/images/work/culia-public-home.png"
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="chip chip--real">Live client project</span>
      <div class="page-head__grid mt-2">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Case study / Automotive retail</p>
          <h1 class="h1">Culia Autos</h1>
        </div>
        <p class="lede">
          A vehicle discovery and consultation platform for a Lagos car
          dealership, with a public website and an admin system the client uses to
          run inventory, bookings and customer interest after handover.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="fact-row">
        <div class="fact">
          <div class="fact__label">Client</div>
          <div class="fact__value">Culia Autos, Lagos</div>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
          <div class="fact__label">Status</div>
          <div class="fact__value">Live in production</div>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
          <div class="fact__label">Scope</div>
          <div class="fact__value">Website, admin, payments, handover</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="btn-row">
        <a
          class="btn btn--primary"
          href="https://www.culiaautos.com/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          Visit the live site <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span>
        </a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/contact">Discuss similar work</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container">
      <Shot
        src="/images/work/culia-public-home.png"
        alt="Culia Autos production homepage with a blue banner, Find My Car, Browse Cars and Book a Consultation buttons, and featured vehicle cards"
        caption="Production homepage. Vehicle discovery is the first action, with consultation booking kept visible in the header on every page."
        tag="Production site"
        wide
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container split">
      <div class="sticky-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Overview</p>
        <h2 class="h2">A showroom that stays current.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Culia Autos sells cars in Lagos. Buyers need to see what is genuinely
          available, understand the condition and specification, and speak to
          someone without a long chain of messages. The dealership needs the same
          inventory to be easy to maintain, and a reliable record of the people
          who are interested.
        </p>
        <p>
          Forthmark Systems designed and built a public vehicle discovery site and
          the operational admin system behind it. The public side handles browsing,
          saving, comparison and paid consultation booking. The admin side handles
          listings, images, shop order, bookings, leads, saved interest and payment
          status.
        </p>
        <p>
          The project was delivered as one connected product rather than a website
          with a separate spreadsheet behind it. That is what makes handover
          practical: the client updates the inventory once, and the public site
          reflects it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--paper2">
    <div class="container split">
      <div class="sticky-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">The challenge</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Interest was real. The process around it was manual.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Car buyers rarely decide in one visit. They compare a few options, ask
          about condition and mileage, save the ones they like, and come back
          later. When that happens across phone calls and messaging apps, details
          get lost and the team cannot tell which cars are attracting serious
          interest.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            The public inventory had to be easy to keep current, including cars
            that were reserved or sold.
          </li>
          <li>
            Buyers needed a clearer way to narrow the catalogue, revisit saved
            cars and compare options side by side.
          </li>
          <li>
            Consultation bookings needed a schedule, a record of the topic, and a
            payment step that reduced casual no-shows.
          </li>
          <li>
            The client needed to run routine updates without asking a developer
            each time a price changed or a car was sold.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="section-head__copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Customer experience</p>
          <h2 class="h2">Browse, narrow down, book.</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            The public site is built around the way a buyer actually shops. Each
            screen has one clear next action, and the same actions remain usable on
            a phone.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid--3">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Find and filter</h3>
          <p>
            Search by make or model, then narrow by price, condition, body, gear,
            fuel and location. A guided Find My Car flow collects budget, purpose
            and passenger needs.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Save and compare</h3>
          <p>
            Signed in customers can save cars and compare up to three at once.
            Comparison puts price, year, condition, mileage, body, engine,
            drivetrain and location in one table.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Book with intent</h3>
          <p>
            Buyers choose a consultation topic, date and time, then pay the fee
            before the booking is confirmed. The record includes the topic and
            contact details for the team.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="gallery mt-3">
        <Shot
          src="/images/work/culia-public-inventory.png"
          alt="Culia Autos Browse Cars page with search, price, condition and body filters, and vehicle cards with View Car and Compare buttons"
          caption="Browse Cars. Filters are visible rather than hidden behind a search box, and the saved state is available on each card."
          tag="Production site"
        />
        <Shot
          src="/images/work/culia-public-car-detail-details.png"
          alt="Culia Autos vehicle detail page showing price, specification table, an unconfirmed specification warning, and inspection and consultation buttons"
          caption="Vehicle detail with a specification table, a clear warning when specs are unconfirmed, and inspection and consultation actions."
          tag="Production site"
        />
        <Shot
          src="/images/work/culia-public-saved.png"
          alt="Culia Autos saved cars page showing three saved vehicles with View Car and Compare buttons"
          caption="Saved cars. The account shown is a fictional demo account; the vehicle listings are from the live catalogue."
          tag="Demo account"
        />
        <Shot
          src="/images/work/culia-public-compare.png"
          alt="Culia Autos comparison table showing three vehicles side by side with price, year, condition, body, drivetrain and location"
          caption="Comparison of up to three vehicles, with differences visible in one table."
          tag="Production site"
        />
        <Shot
          src="/images/work/culia-public-consult.png"
          alt="Culia Autos consultation booking page with topic selector and a November 2026 date calendar"
          caption="Consultation booking starts with the topic and date. Closed days are visibly unavailable."
          tag="Production site"
        />
        <Shot
          src="/images/work/culia-public-consult-calendar.png"
          alt="Culia Autos consultation form showing contact fields, a consultation fee and a Pay 10,000 Naira and Book button"
          caption="The fee and the rule that a booking only counts after payment are stated before checkout."
          tag="Production site"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--paper2">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="section-head__copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Admin and CMS</p>
          <h2 class="h2">The client can run the day to day.</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            The admin system is custom built for Culia's workflow. It is not a
            generic CMS, so the screens use the language of the business: cars,
            shop order, bookings, interest and leads.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid--3">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Inventory</h3>
          <p>
            Add a listing with photos, price, condition, specifications, features
            and status. Edit it later, archive it, or change it to reserved or sold.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Presentation</h3>
          <p>
            Control the order buyers see under Recommended, so the strongest or
            most current stock is not buried by the newest upload date.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Workflow</h3>
          <p>
            Review bookings with their date, time, topic, payment status and
            outcome notes. See saved interest and abandoned booking intents.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="callout callout--concept mt-3">
        <p>
          <strong>About these admin screenshots.</strong> They were captured from a
          local copy of the admin system populated with fictional demo records. The
          interface is the real implementation. Names, phone numbers, emails,
          booking references and amounts are demo data. No production customer or
          payment data is shown.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="gallery mt-3">
        <Shot
          src="/images/work/culia-admin-dashboard.png"
          alt="Culia Autos admin dashboard with available, reserved and sold car totals, upcoming bookings and new leads"
          caption="Admin dashboard: stock totals, upcoming bookings, leads by source and the newest leads that need a call."
          tag="Demo data"
        />
        <Shot
          src="/images/work/culia-admin-vehicles.png"
          alt="Culia Autos admin car list with search, reorder, add car, edit and archive controls"
          caption="Inventory list with search, add, reorder, edit and archive. Status is shown on each listing."
          tag="Demo data"
        />
        <Shot
          src="/images/work/culia-admin-add-vehicle.png"
          alt="Culia Autos add car form with fields for make, model, price, condition, status, specification and description"
          caption="Add car: a structured listing form rather than free text, which keeps the public pages consistent."
          tag="Demo data"
        />
        <Shot
          src="/images/work/culia-admin-edit-vehicle.png"
          alt="Culia Autos edit car screen showing an existing Toyota Tacoma listing with price, status and specification fields"
          caption="Edit car: the same form handles routine changes, including status changes to reserved or sold."
          tag="Demo data"
        />
        <Shot
          src="/images/work/culia-admin-reorder.png"
          alt="Culia Autos shop order screen with numbered vehicle rows and move up and move down buttons"
          caption="Shop order: the client controls the order buyers see. New cars appear at the end until positioned."
          tag="Demo data"
        />
        <Shot
          src="/images/work/culia-admin-bookings.png"
          alt="Culia Autos bookings list showing dates, times, topics, fictional customer names, paid status and outcome fields"
          caption="Bookings schedule: date, time, topic, customer, payment status, booking status and outcome notes."
          tag="Demo data"
        />
        <Shot
          src="/images/work/culia-admin-interest.png"
          alt="Culia Autos interest screen listing which fictional customers saved which cars, and abandoned booking attempts"
          caption="Interest: who saved which cars, plus visitors who picked a time but did not complete payment."
          tag="Demo data"
        />
        <Shot
          src="/images/work/culia-admin-leads.png"
          alt="Culia Autos leads list with fictional customer names, phone numbers, lead source, status and follow up dates"
          caption="Leads: source, status and follow up date, so enquiries are not lost between calls."
          tag="Demo data"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Handover</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Less dependence on the developer.</h2>
        <p class="lede mt-1">
          The admin system is designed for handover, not for a technical operator.
          Routine work is grouped where the team expects it, destructive actions
          are deliberate, and saved changes give immediate feedback.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>Add a vehicle, upload images and publish it to the site.</li>
          <li>Edit price, description, specification or status at any time.</li>
          <li>Reorder the shop so the right cars lead the catalogue.</li>
          <li>Mark a car reserved or sold, or archive it entirely.</li>
          <li>Review the consultation schedule and update booking outcomes.</li>
          <li>See which customers saved a car and follow up with interested buyers.</li>
          <li>See whether a consultation fee was paid, and the amount recorded.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="callout mt-2">
          <p>
            <strong>What still needs Forthmark:</strong> new integrations,
            structural changes to the data model, pricing or booking rule changes,
            and major design work. Routine content and operations do not.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--paper2">
    <div class="container split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Payments</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Payment collection, not accounting.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Paystack is used to collect the consultation fee at the point of
          booking. The payment is verified server side before a booking is
          accepted, and the admin shows whether a booking is paid and the amount
          recorded.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is not a full accounting or reconciliation system. It does not
          replace settlement reports, refund handling, tax records or a finance
          package. Those remain separate business processes.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Role and technology</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Forthmark's responsibilities.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>Scoping the public journey and the internal admin workflow with the client.</li>
          <li>Interface design and information architecture for both sides of the product.</li>
          <li>Full implementation of the website, admin system and database model.</li>
          <li>Saved cars, comparison, consultation booking and payment verification.</li>
          <li>Optional Google Calendar and Meet links for confirmed consultations.</li>
          <li>Testing, deployment and preparation of the admin system for handover.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="callout mt-2">
          <p>
            <strong>Technology note.</strong> Next.js and TypeScript, PostgreSQL,
            Paystack for payment collection and verification, Cloudflare R2 for
            vehicle image storage, Resend for transactional email, and optional
            Google Calendar integration. Admin access is role based, with separate
            super admin, sales and content permissions.
          </p>
        </div>
        <p class="small mt-2">
          No admin credentials, customer records, payment references or private
          system settings are published on this page.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    title="Need a public site and a system behind it?"
    text="We build the customer facing experience and the operational tools together, so updates happen once and the business sees the same truth."
    primaryLabel="Discuss a project"
    secondaryLabel="Explore services"
    secondaryHref="/services"
  />
</BaseLayout>
